{
  "id": "nalmefene",
  "term": "nalmefene",
  "definition": "Nalmefene is a small-molecule mu opioid receptor antagonist that is used as an antidote for fentanyl and related opioid overdose. It is structurally similar to naloxone but has a much longer elimination half-life in humans, about 11 hours, which may help extend reversal of opioid effects.",
